e82a8d04ed7b54dd61b6f3fea90953de9.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Advisory","headline":"Flood Advisory issued August 15 at 4:48PM MDT until August 15 at 7:45PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is expected.\n\n* WHERE...Northwestern Logan County in northeastern Colorado...\nNortheastern Weld County in northeastern Colorado...\n\n* WHEN...Until 745 PM MDT.\n\n* IMPACTS...Minor flooding in low-lying and poor drainage areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n\n- At 448 PM MDT, Doppler radar indicated heavy rain due to\nthunderstorms. Minor flooding is ongoing or expected to begin\nshortly in the advisory area. Between 0.5 and 1.5 inches of rain\nhave fallen.\n\n- Additional rainfall amounts up to 1 inch are expected over the\narea. This additional rain will result in minor flooding.\n\n- Some locations that will experience flooding include...\nWestplains, Pawnee Pass, Logan Corners, Willard, North Sterling\nReservoir and Stoneham.","ends":"2026-08-15T19:45:00-06:00","severity":"Minor","areaDesc":"Logan, CO; Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3f8ef2b5c187439d915089556d8a25535ba19625.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.3f8ef2b5c187439d915089556d8a25535ba19625.001.1"},{"event":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch","headline":"Severe Thunderstorm Watch issued August 15 at 2:05PM MDT until August 15 at 9:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"THE NATIONAL WEATHER SERVICE HAS ISSUED SEVERE THUNDERSTORM WATCH\n584 IN EFFECT UNTIL 9 PM MDT THIS EVENING FOR THE FOLLOWING AREAS\n\nIN COLORADO THIS WATCH INCLUDES 9 COUNTIES\n\nIN EAST CENTRAL COLORADO\n\nELBERT                LINCOLN\n\nIN NORTHEAST COLORADO\n\nADAMS                 ARAPAHOE              DOUGLAS\nLOGAN                 MORGAN                WASHINGTON\nWELD\n\nTHIS INCLUDES THE CITIES OF AKRON, AURORA, CASTLE ROCK,\nCENTENNIAL, ELIZABETH, FORT MORGAN, GREELEY, KIOWA, LIMON,\nPARKER, STERLING, THORNTON, WESTMINSTER, AND WINDSOR.","ends":"2026-08-15T21:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Adams, CO; Arapahoe, CO; Douglas, CO; Elbert, CO; Lincoln, CO; Logan, CO; Morgan, CO; Washington, CO; Weld, CO","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.862838f8b61c9032ddaddac2ecfc011791cca58a.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.862838f8b61c9032ddaddac2ecfc011791cca58a.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued August 15 at 11:52AM MDT until August 15 at 10:00PM MDT by NWS Denver CO","description":"* WHAT...Flash Flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of central and northeast Colorado, including the\nfollowing areas: the southern Front Range Foothills, Palmer Divide\narea, I-25 corridor, and all of our eastern plains counties.\n\n* WHEN...Until 10 PM MDT this evening.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nFlooding may occur in poor drainage and urban areas.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- Additional thunderstorms and heavy rainfall this afternoon,\ncombined with the heavy rainfall from the past 3 days, will bring\na threat for flash flooding this afternoon and evening. Stronger\nstorms will be capable of producing 1 to 2 inches of rain in 30\nminutes, with isolated areas receiving storm totals of 2 to 4\ninches.","ends":"2026-08-15T22:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Jefferson and West Douglas Counties Above  6000 Feet/Gilpin/Clear Creek/Northeast Park Counties Below 9000 Feet; Larimer County Below 6000 Feet/Northwest Weld County; Boulder And Jefferson Counties Below 6000 Feet/West Broomfield County; North Douglas County Below 6000 Feet/Denver/West Adams and Arapahoe Counties/East Broomfield County; Elbert/Central and East Douglas Counties Above 6000 Feet; Northeast Weld County; Central and South Weld County; Morgan County; Central and East Adams and Arapahoe Counties; North and Northeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/North Lincoln County; Southeast Elbert County Below 6000 Feet/South Lincoln County; Logan County; Washington County; Sedgwick County; Phillips County","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eea7fe66bbe726127cab571e453d260029b0d72c.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.eea7fe66bbe726127cab571e453d260029b0d72c.001.1"},{"event":"Flood Watch","headline":"Flood Watch issued August 15 at 11:32AM MDT until August 16 at 6:00AM MDT by NWS Goodland KS","description":"* WHAT...Flash flooding caused by excessive rainfall is possible.\n\n* WHERE...Portions of east central Colorado, including the following\narea, Cheyenne CO and west central Kansas, including the following\nareas, Gove, Greeley, Logan, Wallace and Wichita.\n\n* WHEN...From 6 PM MDT  /7 PM CDT/ this evening through late tonight.\n\n* IMPACTS...Excessive runoff may result in flooding of rivers,\ncreeks, streams, and other low-lying and flood-prone locations.\nLow-water crossings may be flooded.\n\n* ADDITIONAL DETAILS...\n- 1-3 inches of rain the past couple nights along with the\npotential for another cluster or two of storms this evening and\novernight increases the potential for some flooding and even\nflash flooding. Rainfall rates of 1.5 to 2.5 inches per hour is\npossible in the strongest cells.","ends":"2026-08-16T06:00:00-06:00","severity":"Severe","areaDesc":"Cheyenne County; Wallace; Logan; Gove; Greeley; Wichita","id":"urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e088e0765aa75bc050e847f792689803d87d9b3f.001.1","url":"https://api.weather.gov/alerts/urn:oid:2.49.0.1.840.0.e088e0765aa75bc050e847f792689803d87d9b3f.001.1"}],"afd":{"office":"PUB","issued":"2026-08-15T23:41:00+00:00","snippet":"000 FXUS65 KPUB 152341 AFDPUB Area Forecast Discussion National Weather Service Pueblo CO 541 PM MDT Sat Aug 15 2026 .KEY MESSAGES... - Thunderstorms capable of producing heavy rainfall and flash flooding continue through Sunday with a few strong to severe thunderstorms across the southeast plains both days. - Thunderstorm activity a little less wide